    "response_text": "Database indexes play a crucial role in optimizing data retrieval processes within relational databases. An index is essentially a sorted list of records that can be used to quickly locate specific rows based on certain criteria. The most common type of index is the B-tree index, which is widely used across various database systems.\n\nA B-tree index works by organizing data into a tree-like structure where each node contains multiple keys (or values) and pointers to other nodes. This allows for efficient searching, insertion, and deletion operations. When a user queries the database using an indexed field, the system first checks if the query matches any of the leaf nodes in the B-tree",
